<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Bearing Man yr shr dips, div up.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Bearing Man yr shr dips, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre-excepts	   25.7  vs  26.5</p>
<p>    - post-excepts	  25.7  vs  26.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 10.7  vs  10.5</p>
<p>    Taxed earnings	  27.05 vs  27.33</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   39.20 vs  41.92</p>
<p>    Tax			 12.16 vs  14.59</p>
<p>    Interest cost	   11.60 vs   6.82</p>
<p>    Turnover		 357.59 vs 310.43</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	--   vs   0.3 loss</p>
<p>Div payable: August 29</p>
<p>On register: August 15</p>
<p>Full name: Bearing Man Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The engineering firm said comparative figures had been restated, where applicable, to reflect the February 1997 share increase, an effective ten-for-one sub-division of its issued shares. This had necessitated the reporting of earnings and dividends per share to the nearest decimal point.</p>
<p>It said it expected earnings to increase in the 1998 financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
